    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pescennĭus</span></b> , i,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name
				of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A friend of Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				14, 4, 6</span></i>.—Esp., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Pescennius Niger, <i>a Roman emperor;</i> hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pescenniānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>pertaining to the emperor
				Pescennius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reliquiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Spart. Sev. 15, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Pesc. Nig. 12, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
